   "why": "a residual-stream permutation permutes a reader's columns and a writer's rows; R3 searches one scale per output row over (weight, act_rms) pairs, so both are invariant IN THE WEIGHTS. It is not invariant in the CALIBRATION: the forward pass sums squares over permuted channels, act_rms differs in its last bits, and a near-tie in the scale search can flip a code. Judged at 0.2 sigma_seed, not at fp round-off. A value LARGER than that is a bug in the rotation machinery."
